OpenVMS Track

The OpenVMS Track will provide intermediate to advanced technical
practitioners, system managers, and IT designers and planners with the
latest how-to information and solutions for maximizing current and planned
investments in OpenVMS.

Solution-focused sessions, along with hands on workshops, will go beyond
product speeds and feeds to address the deployment of this information to
solve real-life enterprise computing needs today. Hints and Kinks sessions
will provide a chance for attendees to engage in technical discussions with
OpenVMS engineers.

Sessions will address such issues as how to have a headache-free January 1st
in the Year 2000, and how to web-enable and access distributed OpenVMS data.
Attendees will learn how to take advantage of advanced file sharing and data
storage capabilities, how to maximize system resources with Galaxy, and how
to enable continuous computing with OpenVMS and Windows NT. There will also
be sessions on how to design and implement disaster tolerant systems, how to
deploy and manage OpenVMS clusters, and how to manage OpenVMS from Windows
NT, as well as technical update sessions on OpenVMS and the OpenVMS/Affinity
for NT Program.

Hands-on sessions include:
1) Building and using a cluster,
2) NT Integration with PATHWORKS.







