Wednesday, April 8, 1998

Do You Have a TruCluster, Or Just a Clump?

This day is dedicated to highly available TruCluster installations.  From
the engineers who invented clusters, you will be learning about the issues
of planning, installing and tuning which revolve around the type of load you
have on the system, and engineering will address different types of load.
For instance, does the sendmail lock files have performance problems when
running under NFS?  How can you tune the cluster software to give you good
database performance even in a fail-over situation?

So in this day�s discussions, the engineers will cover:
? Definition of a cluster, and cluster components
? Setting up a highly available server
? Tuning a highly available server
? Issues around: NFS servers,
   database engineers,
   datamining,
    web servers
? Mastering the Memory Channel

The aspects of setting up a high performance clustered (HPC) system will be
covered in a separate session.







