TU003:  "Using Clustering for High Availability and Performance with
Digital UNIX" -- JUMP START

Instructor: Brad Nichols

Mr. Nichols is the UNIX Systems Curriculum Architect at ISA. He is directly
responsible for course development and trainer supervision in this arena.

Some of Brad's recent software projects include the following:
Designed and authored ISA�s Digital UNIX Internals Course and is currently
writing a hands-on Windows NT Architecture Course. Developed a TruCluster
Application Programming Course that teaches Distributed Parallel Processing.


Format:        One Day Demonstration/Workstation -- JUMP Start

Prerequisites: DIGITAL UNIX System Administration
UNIX Network Management

Objective:
To meet application uptime and performance requirements multiple
DIGITAL UNIX systems can be clustered using the TruCluster product from
DIGITAL.

This seminar reviews the goals of High Availability and Parallel Performance
of clustering, describes the features of the TruCluster product and how they
can be used to meet these goals for a wide range of applications.

After describing hardware and software configuration, the instructor will
demonstrate the related tools and the operations of the associated system
administration activities on a complete TruCluster configuration.

In the afternoon session, you will create an NFS Service and run it on a
TruCluster System.

After the class, the students will understand the hardware configuration,
Software installation, and failover processes. They will be able to create
an NFS service with failover capability.








