TU006:  Configuring Digital UNIX as a Webserver

Instructor: Pravin Munakur

Pravin V. Mundkur is an Independent Contractor at SoftCel. He
develops and instructs training at The Institute for Software
Advancement, Northeastern University, and other Boston area
Universities.  His areas of interest include Internet
Architecture; Internet Server and Client Programming; Java
Programming; C++ Programming; Windows Programming; and
Client/Server Programming.

Pravin spent ten years at Digital, where he served in several
capacities in the Software Engineering area. He also has provided consulting
on Digital Operating Systems, Network and Database products.

Some of Pravin's most recent developments at SoftCel include: Set up of WEB
access to database systems; Wrote a web based trivia game; Developed a
customer service web application; Developed a Visual Basic front end for SQL
Server/UNIX based MRP application; Wrote Visual Basic custom controls in
Visual C; Developed DOS and Windows front ends in Microsoft C/ C++;
Developed interfaces from mail front end to PC databases; Helped to
implement DECnet Phase IV and TCP/IP network management support in FDDI
bridge and routing products; Implemented a forms oriented system and print
management tool.

Format: Lecture/Lab Seminar

Audience:
System Administrators planing to configure and manage Digital UNIX platforms
as a Webservers.

Prerequisites:
Familiarity with UNIX Base System Administration, TCP/IP Protocols and
Network Administration

Objective:
Everyone from grade school students to CEOs want to get a web pages up on
the net and as a System Administrator you are or will be called on to make
it happen. Digital UNIX is a great platform to use as a Webserver due to its
high performance, sophisticated server software such as TruClusters and the
available Webserver Software such as Netscape FastTrack.  Whether you plan
to add a Webserver to an existing platform or to configure a new dedicated
high-performance highly available server this seminar will prepare you.

The tutorial covers:
? A background section on general Webserver concepts and issues such as
HTML, CGI, Java, IP Addressing and Virtual Hosting
? A description of Webserver features of Digital UNIX,  Apache Webserver and
Netscape Webserver.
? Detail coverage of the installation, configuration, tuning and  management
of Netscape FastTrack Webserver on DIGITAL UNIX

A Lab section is included where students will install and configure Netscape
FastTrack on DIGITAL UNIX. Students will get a hands on familiarity with
installation tools, Administration Server and command-line configuration
tools, debugging and tuning tools.







